def is_prime(n):
    if n < 2:
        return False
    for I in range(2, int(n**0.5)+1):
        if n % I == 0:
            return False
    return True

This function takes an integer n as input and returns True if n is prime, and False otherwise. It first checks if n is less than 2, which are not prime numbers. Then, it loops through all integers from 2 to the square root of n (rounded up) and checks if n is divisible by any of them. If n is divisible by any of them, it is not prime and the function returns False. Otherwise, it is prime and the function returns True.```

